1
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:09,200
- You want to audition as a singer here?
- Yes.

2
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:12,320
<i>I suppose this is one way</i>
<i>for you to convince Phatee</i>

3
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:13,600
<i>to take your job, right?</i>

4
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:16,079
- Do you trust me?
- I trust you.

5
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:17,440
<i>Then I'm sorry in advance.</i>

6
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:18,880
<i>You're pretty naughty.</i>

7
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:20,200
Incense doesn't work on you,

8
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:21,720
<i>but the moment we kissed, you showed up.</i>

9
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:23,520
<i>Vann!</i>

10
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:24,720
I'm not afraid of ghosts.

11
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,640
<i>I'm more afraid of not being with you.</i>

12
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:30,240
Garlah said my life
would be ruined because of a man.

13
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:32,479
So she doesn't like you dating men.

14
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:34,120
<i>Where are you?</i>

15
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,920
<i>Come out and talk to me.</i>

16
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:56,240
Where are you?

17
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:57,760
Come out and talk to me.

18
00:00:58,960 --> 00:00:59,760
Stop hiding.

19
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:01,840
You come into my dreams
almost every night.

20
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:03,560
Just coming out to talk to me

21
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:04,680
can't be that hard, right?

22
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:10,720
I know you're around here.

23
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:13,080
Aren't you protective of Rakkhun anymore?

24
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:35,320
Okay.

25
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:36,800
Now it'll be easier for us to talk.

26
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:38,640
Let's make a deal.

27
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:41,880
Are you sure you want to do this?

28
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:44,080
I'm sure.

29
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:45,280
Or I wouldn't have summoned you.

30
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:47,120
You have issues. I understand.

31
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:48,840
But don't give other people issues too.

32
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:50,560
What era are we living in?

33
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:51,960
People accept it now.

34
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:54,040
Rakkhun's life won't be like yours.

35
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:56,200
How can you be sure

36
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:59,680
Rakkhun won't end up like me?

37
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:02,080
Then how about this?

38
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:04,120
I'll guarantee it.

39
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:05,960
If you let Rakkhun go

40
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:08,080
and his life falls apart
because he's dating Kan,

41
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:10,720
- I'll take responsibility.
- How will you do that?

42
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:15,320
Anything.

43
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:16,600
Name it.

44
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:19,400
Your life.

45
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:24,920
If Rakkhun gets his heart broken,

46
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,560
you die!

47
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:28,920
You want my life?

48
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,760
Otherwise, Rakkhun must
live the life I want.

49
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:40,360
If it costs me my life,

50
00:02:40,440 --> 00:02:41,920
you'll disappear for good

51
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,840
and never make things
hard for him again, right?

52
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:45,400
Yes.

53
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:48,480
But if Rakkhun

54
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:52,000
gets his heart broken from dating a man,

55
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:54,080
you must die!

56
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:04,720
Okay.

57
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:10,520
If you change your mind
and want to cancel the deal,

58
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:13,640
there's nothing you can do to change it.

59
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:16,200
I always keep my word.

60
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,720
Then from now on,

61
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:21,680
your life

62
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:23,240
belongs to me.

63
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:48,160
I'm afraid that

64
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:50,960
if we're too close,
the ghost will show up.

65
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,120
Then…

66
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:00,880
shall we test it?

67
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:02,760
See if the ghost shows up.

68
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:09,600
What are you doing?

69
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:12,280
Well, I'm testing it

70
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:14,080
to see if the ghost shows up.

71
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:20,200
I don't think you should risk it.

72
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:30,600
Thank you.

73
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:32,000
You can head back now.

74
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:56,400
We're closed.

75
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Vann.

76
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:03,800
Rakkhun.

77
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:05,040
How did you get here?

78
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:27,720
Did you see Garlah?

79
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:29,760
Did Garlah come out?

80
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:33,840
What exactly did you come here to do?

81
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:35,800
When I was with Kan,

82
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:37,440
Garlah didn't show up.

83
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:39,720
I thought she might be gone,

84
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:41,480
so I came to test it with you.

85
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:45,720
So that kiss was you testing it?

86
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:47,880
I don't think that's appropriate.

87
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:49,480
Next time, test it with Kan.

88
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:51,600
What are you annoyed about?

89
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:54,480
You kissed me to lure Garlah out before.

90
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,880
Well, it's my job.

91
00:06:56,960 --> 00:06:59,600
So, you really didn't see Garlah?

92
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:02,840
Let me try again,
in case she didn't see it.

93
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:04,680
I don't think she's coming anymore.

94
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:07,600
How do you know that?

95
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:10,280
I've already talked to her.

96
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:12,160
I told you I could do it.

97
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:14,080
Are you sure?

98
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:17,040
She won't come back
and snap your neck later, right?

99
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,840
As long as she's gone,
you're okay with that, right?

100
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:23,200
I did it.

101
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:24,720
I kept my promise exactly.

102
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:27,080
From now on, you can
live however you want.

103
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,680
You can have a boyfriend

104
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:30,120
or enjoy yourself.

105
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:31,120
You can fall in love.

106
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:33,000
Whatever you want to do, you can do it.

107
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:37,200
Aren't you happy?

108
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:39,000
This is what you wanted.

109
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:41,080
What about what you want?

110
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:45,400
What I want is to finish the job.

111
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:47,560
Job done, I get paid.

112
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:49,840
Then I can go study like I planned.

113
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:52,800
Soon you'll have to call me an engineer.

114
00:07:53,520 --> 00:07:56,120
That's really all you want, right?

115
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:58,640
You've never wanted anything else from me?

116
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:09,400
Yes.

117
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:12,280
I'm here because I need the money.

118
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:18,240
Okay.

119
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:21,040
Then I'll consider this job finished.

120
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:32,679
I'm glad I met you, Vann.

121
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:39,080
Thanks for everything.

122
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:15,200
It's better to end it this way, right?

123
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:40,720
<i>Vann, are you up?</i>

124
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:52,360
<i>Rakkhun, what are you doing?</i>

125
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,000
Want some?

126
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:42,560
Mimi, put it over there.

127
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:47,960
Hey!

128
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:50,520
Vann, what's wrong?

129
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:52,480
You keep sitting there sighing.

130
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:55,320
With symptoms like this,

131
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:57,400
I give it a ten out of ten.

132
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,600
He's definitely heartbroken.

133
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:00,800
Heartbroken?

134
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:02,400
Who broke your heart?

135
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:04,600
Tell me. I'll go beat them up.

136
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:07,520
How dare they break your heart
when all you've got is your good looks?

137
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:10,800
Tangmo, are you insulting him?

138
00:11:13,040 --> 00:11:14,520
Are you heartbroken over Rakkhun?

139
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:17,960
Rakkhun?

140
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:19,520
The one who came to me for a reading?

141
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:20,880
Stop it.

142
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:22,240
I'm not heartbroken.

143
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:23,880
I just haven't slept much.

144
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:25,840
- That's all.
- "Haven't slept much."

145
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:39,240
One million just hit your account!

146
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:41,040
Vann, Rakkhun paid you that much?

147
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:42,960
You finished the job already?

148
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:44,840
I did.

149
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:46,560
We don't have to see each other anymore.

150
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:50,600
If you're not happy,

151
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:51,920
just give the money back.

152
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,920
You got that much money,

153
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,760
so why aren't you happy
like you usually are?

154
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:01,120
Are you going to study abroad right away?

155
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:02,640
You've got all the money now.

156
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:04,480
I've already applied.

157
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:06,600
I planned to leave as soon as
this job was done.

158
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:07,680
Hey, Vann.

159
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:09,200
Why so sudden?

160
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:11,000
You didn't tell us anything.

161
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:12,640
Exactly.

162
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:15,160
Won't you stay and save up
some pocket money first?

163
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:19,040
Sooner or later, he has to go anyway.

164
00:12:19,560 --> 00:12:21,120
Good luck, Vann.

165
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:23,600
Hey.

166
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:25,800
We should be happy for him.

167
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:27,160
He gets to continue his studies

168
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:28,960
and pursue his dream.

169
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:34,360
Then, if there's anything
we can help with,

170
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:35,600
just let us know.

171
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:38,120
Except money.

172
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,320
Thank you so much.

173
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:43,600
Thank you, everyone.

174
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:47,880
Thank you too, Linda.

175
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:50,200
I couldn't have done it without you.

176
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:52,800
Hey, Vann.

177
00:12:52,880 --> 00:12:54,520
Give yourself some credit.

178
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:57,200
I just brought you the job.

179
00:12:57,280 --> 00:13:00,040
You finished it yourself.

180
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:03,400
Irasshaimase.

181
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:06,440
Hai! Vann-san.

182
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:08,480
Hey.

183
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:10,240
Don't forget our souvenirs.

184
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:11,640
- Got it?
- Hey.

185
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:13,080
My skincare and makeup too.

186
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:15,040
- I messaged you. Read it.
- And my mochi.

187
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:18,040
- I want the real thing.
- You can eat mochi in Nakhon Sawan.

188
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:19,840
I don't care. But tonight,

189
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:21,000
Vann's treating us.

190
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:23,040
- Vann's treating us!
- Really?

191
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:25,360
How about Omakase?
I want it. I've never had it.

192
00:13:25,440 --> 00:13:27,160
- Yeah, you got a whole million.
- Please?

193
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:31,160
- Treat us. It's not that expensive.
- You're treating all of us.

194
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:50,400
Customers aren't allowed back here.

195
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:54,000
I'm not here as a customer.

196
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:58,360
Today I'm here as a singer.

197
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:07,520
You want to sing here?

198
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:11,120
Sorry, I haven't rehearsed
with you at all.

199
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:12,800
You take the lead today.

200
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:14,160
I'll follow you.

201
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:20,160
We sing with our backs
to the audience, right?

202
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:22,480
Doing this

203
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:24,760
won't get you an answer
from me any faster.

204
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:30,680
You're used to your comfort zone,
aren't you?

205
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:32,960
But it's okay.

206
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:36,120
I'll let you test the system on me first.

207
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:39,160
If we end up in the same band,

208
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:41,280
we'll have to sing together, right?

209
00:14:42,560 --> 00:14:44,960
I think singing here first is a good idea.

210
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:47,160
Then I'll know if our voices
work together.

211
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:52,480
Who said I'd sing with you?

212
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:56,560
We're singing separately for an hour each.

213
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:59,280
Wait.

214
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:01,000
Wait, wait, wait.

215
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:03,280
I was hired to perform as a duo,

216
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:05,040
not solo.

217
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:06,120
No.

218
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:11,320
Hey.

219
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:13,320
Are you scared of me or something?

220
00:15:14,200 --> 00:15:16,680
Afraid you'll lose fans
if you perform with me?

221
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:19,480
If it works,

222
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:21,760
then you can consider my offer.

223
00:15:21,840 --> 00:15:23,960
But if it doesn't,
we'll go our separate ways.

224
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:26,440
I won't bug you again.

225
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:30,240
Okay?

226
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,960
Not working today, Mr. Writer?

227
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:58,040
No.

228
00:15:58,120 --> 00:15:59,480
I just want to drink today.

229
00:16:04,760 --> 00:16:05,880
I can order myself.

230
00:16:06,680 --> 00:16:08,240
Consider it on the house.

231
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:10,400
You're paying our bar anyway.

232
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:15,520
Has work been too much lately?

233
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:18,000
You look sleep-deprived.

234
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:21,480
I haven't been sleeping well.

235
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:23,080
Thoughts keep running through my head.

236
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,160
If you'd agreed to help from the start,

237
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:26,440
I wouldn't be this exhausted.

238
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:29,520
Is overthinking normal for writers?

239
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:31,720
You could say it's normal,

240
00:16:31,800 --> 00:16:33,880
but you could also say it's not.

241
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:36,520
Anyway, I'm fine.

242
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,600
I'll drink until I black out.

243
00:16:38,680 --> 00:16:39,920
Then I'll fall asleep.

244
00:16:46,840 --> 00:16:48,520
Then I'll drink with you tonight.

245
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:00,280
Wouldn't it be better
to hire someone else?

246
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:02,920
Then let me ask you.

247
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:05,200
When choosing a boyfriend,
what do you look for?

248
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:07,440
If he makes a good first impression,

249
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:08,560
I go talk to him.

250
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:10,680
If we click, I'll give it a shot.

251
00:17:11,359 --> 00:17:13,119
If we don't, we go our separate ways.

252
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:14,599
No strings attached.

253
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:15,680
Simple as that.

254
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:18,800
But it can't be just anyone, right?

255
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:20,880
The male lead in my novel is the same.

256
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:22,560
I already picture him as you.

257
00:17:22,640 --> 00:17:23,960
It has to be you.

258
00:17:26,520 --> 00:17:28,520
You don't even know me that well.

259
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:30,520
My looks

260
00:17:30,600 --> 00:17:32,120
might be fooling you.

261
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:33,680
Inside,

262
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:36,120
I'm far from what you think.

263
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:38,560
Can't help it.

264
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:40,360
I've already decided

265
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:41,600
to wait for you to change your mind.

266
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:46,080
That day will never come, Mr. Writer.

267
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:49,920
But if it's
a different kind of relationship…

268
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:53,360
I could be down.

269
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:44,720
Ready?

270
00:18:47,800 --> 00:18:48,800
Come on.

271
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:55,000
What's with you? Show me some effort.

272
00:18:57,800 --> 00:18:58,800
Are you okay?

273
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:01,000
Whoa.

274
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:08,320
Yoyeh.

275
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:48,400
<i>At this rate, you won't get ten million.</i>

276
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:51,000
That's why I'm here practicing with you.

277
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:53,400
You still have time.

278
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:56,160
Besides,

279
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:59,120
I already have you helping me.

280
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:01,880
How do you know I'll help you?

281
00:20:02,560 --> 00:20:05,120
Taking your job doesn't mean
I'll help you.

282
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:07,720
I might just go for a stroll

283
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:09,840
and wait to get paid.

284
00:20:11,160 --> 00:20:13,120
Are you just fucking with me

285
00:20:14,360 --> 00:20:16,800
or making excuses to spend time with me?

286
00:20:18,920 --> 00:20:20,680
You're full of yourself, aren't you?

287
00:20:25,520 --> 00:20:27,320
I'm not.

288
00:20:28,520 --> 00:20:30,240
But it's obvious from how you're acting.

289
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:49,200
I'm going back to work.

290
00:20:50,280 --> 00:20:51,280
Time's up.

291
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:53,320
Let's train again later.

292
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:55,760
See you. Bye.

293
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:01,640
Is it really that obvious?

294
00:21:07,880 --> 00:21:09,240
Vann isn't here.

295
00:21:12,760 --> 00:21:14,240
Have a seat.

296
00:21:18,440 --> 00:21:19,680
Where did Vann go?

297
00:21:21,880 --> 00:21:23,080
He's not here anymore.

298
00:21:24,360 --> 00:21:26,400
You mean he's already
gone abroad to study?

299
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:28,080
Why didn't he tell me anything?

300
00:21:29,080 --> 00:21:30,720
He just went back to his mother's house.

301
00:21:31,280 --> 00:21:33,960
He hasn't gone to Japan yet.
Don't look so shocked.

302
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:36,720
But, oh, well,

303
00:21:37,520 --> 00:21:38,880
good thing you're here.

304
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:41,400
Can you take this book to Vann?

305
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:44,320
At his house.

306
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:55,480
I'll send you the location.

307
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:10,640
Linda.

308
00:22:10,720 --> 00:22:12,560
Didn't you say you love
all the Crows equally?

309
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:14,840
Now you're role-playing Cupid.

310
00:22:15,480 --> 00:22:16,400
Find someone for me too.

311
00:22:16,480 --> 00:22:18,080
You just keep talking nonsense.

312
00:22:18,640 --> 00:22:20,240
Move on from your ex first.

313
00:22:20,320 --> 00:22:22,120
I've moved on.

314
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:23,960
- Really?
- Really!

315
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:49,200
Is Dad helping you?

316
00:22:50,200 --> 00:22:51,240
The lottery results are out.

317
00:22:51,320 --> 00:22:53,320
He's in no mood to help me.

318
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:57,320
Don't tell me you've been
doing this all by yourself.

319
00:22:58,360 --> 00:23:00,760
Well, how else am I supposed
to pay the bills? Look.

320
00:23:00,840 --> 00:23:02,120
The fridge is broken.

321
00:23:02,200 --> 00:23:03,880
The shop isn't doing very well either.

322
00:23:03,960 --> 00:23:05,840
So money's a little tight.

323
00:23:06,520 --> 00:23:07,800
From now on,

324
00:23:07,880 --> 00:23:10,040
save some of the money I send you.

325
00:23:10,120 --> 00:23:12,800
As for the shop,
if you can't manage, close it for now.

326
00:23:12,880 --> 00:23:14,400
Wait until I come back to help you.

327
00:23:16,120 --> 00:23:17,840
Why worry about me now?

328
00:23:17,920 --> 00:23:19,720
I can take care of myself.

329
00:23:22,160 --> 00:23:23,520
Even though I

330
00:23:23,600 --> 00:23:25,400
haven't been a very good mother…

331
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:29,080
It's my first time
having a child, after all.

332
00:23:30,760 --> 00:23:31,760
But you

333
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:34,840
have done so well.

334
00:23:40,720 --> 00:23:42,840
You've really done so well.

335
00:23:50,840 --> 00:23:52,480
Don't get all sentimental on me.

336
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:06,920
TOM YUM NOODLES

337
00:24:08,520 --> 00:24:10,520
- Let's go!
- Let's go.

338
00:24:13,040 --> 00:24:18,320
TOM YUM NOODLES

339
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:20,040
Yo!

340
00:24:20,120 --> 00:24:21,120
How are you?

341
00:24:23,360 --> 00:24:24,400
What's with you guys?

342
00:24:24,480 --> 00:24:25,480
Why are you all here?

343
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:27,640
I'm leaving tomorrow.

344
00:24:29,520 --> 00:24:31,920
Tangmo, didn't you say
he was leaving today?

345
00:24:33,520 --> 00:24:35,000
Did I remember wrong?

346
00:24:36,040 --> 00:24:38,040
But I remember you're leaving today.

347
00:24:38,120 --> 00:24:39,600
Did you remember wrong, Vann?

348
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:41,000
How could I remember wrong?

349
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:42,520
I'm really leaving tomorrow.

350
00:24:45,760 --> 00:24:46,800
So,

351
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:48,480
has anyone come to see you yet?

352
00:24:49,480 --> 00:24:51,320
Who would come see me?

353
00:24:51,400 --> 00:24:52,640
Just you guys.

354
00:24:53,760 --> 00:24:55,400
You really don't have to see me off.

355
00:24:56,120 --> 00:24:57,520
I'll only be gone a few years.

356
00:25:04,480 --> 00:25:05,840
What's wrong?

357
00:25:05,920 --> 00:25:07,120
Why are you crying?

358
00:25:07,200 --> 00:25:09,120
I'm going to study, not to die.

359
00:25:10,240 --> 00:25:13,560
I'm crying because I'm happy

360
00:25:14,240 --> 00:25:15,920
that from now on,

361
00:25:16,520 --> 00:25:17,960
I won't have to hear you

362
00:25:18,040 --> 00:25:22,200
nagging my ears off anymore.

363
00:25:25,440 --> 00:25:27,080
Just admit you'll miss me.

364
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:28,680
Stop crying already.

365
00:25:29,560 --> 00:25:30,600
I'll bring you some skincare.

366
00:25:34,520 --> 00:25:37,520
Then I'll send you pictures.
There's a lot that I want.

367
00:25:38,760 --> 00:25:40,640
Can I message you?

368
00:25:41,320 --> 00:25:42,240
I knew it.

369
00:25:42,840 --> 00:25:45,080
I can't tell if you were crying
or just acting.

370
00:25:46,840 --> 00:25:49,160
- I was really crying, but…
- Okay, okay.

371
00:25:49,680 --> 00:25:50,720
Here.

372
00:25:52,040 --> 00:25:53,600
It's made of lucky stones.

373
00:25:53,680 --> 00:25:56,400
It'll keep you safe from harm.

374
00:25:56,480 --> 00:25:57,680
Give me your arm.

375
00:25:58,520 --> 00:25:59,880
Wear it.

376
00:26:00,880 --> 00:26:01,960
Can you put it on?

377
00:26:04,560 --> 00:26:06,720
I made this myself last night.

378
00:26:06,800 --> 00:26:09,200
See if it really keeps you safe.

379
00:26:10,480 --> 00:26:12,040
Am I your guinea pig?

380
00:26:12,120 --> 00:26:15,200
Let's call you my first customer.

381
00:26:15,920 --> 00:26:16,960
Okay?

382
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:20,280
And I…

383
00:26:20,360 --> 00:26:23,080
I've sent you a list of places to visit.

384
00:26:23,160 --> 00:26:24,480
I'm telling you,

385
00:26:24,560 --> 00:26:26,760
getting some rest is important.

386
00:26:26,840 --> 00:26:28,880
I've picked out a massage place for you.

387
00:26:28,960 --> 00:26:30,520
- Tangmo.
- Tangmo.

388
00:26:36,800 --> 00:26:39,000
Here. Your pocket money.

389
00:26:40,960 --> 00:26:42,240
Hey.

390
00:26:42,320 --> 00:26:43,480
You…

391
00:26:44,280 --> 00:26:46,280
Everyone at the bar chipped in for you.

392
00:26:46,360 --> 00:26:48,440
I just exchanged it for you.

393
00:26:49,920 --> 00:26:52,400
Now that's a heartfelt gift.

394
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:54,200
Thank you!

395
00:26:57,560 --> 00:26:58,840
You're acting like a kid.

396
00:27:02,800 --> 00:27:04,640
- You exchanged it already?
- Yeah.

397
00:27:06,560 --> 00:27:08,080
And before you go,

398
00:27:08,640 --> 00:27:09,880
have you cleared things up with Rakkhun?

399
00:27:19,960 --> 00:27:21,480
I don't know what there is to clear up.

400
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:23,920
The job's done. We go our separate ways.

401
00:27:25,360 --> 00:27:27,080
I'd rather stay single
and focus on studying.

402
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:31,120
Well,

403
00:27:31,720 --> 00:27:32,560
good luck.

404
00:27:36,840 --> 00:27:38,560
Have a safe trip.

405
00:27:39,160 --> 00:27:40,160
Good luck.

406
00:27:41,040 --> 00:27:42,200
Let's hug.

407
00:27:42,800 --> 00:27:44,200
Have a safe trip.

408
00:27:44,280 --> 00:27:45,240
Come on.

409
00:27:45,320 --> 00:27:48,360
- Come on.
- Don't forget the souvenirs you promised.

410
00:27:49,200 --> 00:27:50,120
I know.

411
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:23,000
Rakkhun.

412
00:28:23,920 --> 00:28:24,920
How did you get here?

413
00:28:28,440 --> 00:28:30,440
Linda asked me to return this book to you.

414
00:28:40,520 --> 00:28:42,600
Do you seriously not care about me?

415
00:28:42,680 --> 00:28:44,120
You're leaving tomorrow.

416
00:28:44,880 --> 00:28:46,480
Are you really leaving like this?

417
00:28:52,960 --> 00:28:54,440
Let me ask you honestly.

418
00:28:54,520 --> 00:28:56,680
Have you never felt anything for me?

419
00:29:00,400 --> 00:29:02,400
You're my client.

420
00:29:02,480 --> 00:29:03,960
I don't know if you can tell,

421
00:29:04,040 --> 00:29:05,440
but I'm a professional.

422
00:29:06,760 --> 00:29:08,080
Then when you kissed me,

423
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:09,920
slept with me,

424
00:29:10,960 --> 00:29:11,920
kept messaging me,

425
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:14,040
stayed up all night
building the model for me,

426
00:29:14,760 --> 00:29:16,560
was all of that just for work?

427
00:29:19,440 --> 00:29:21,240
What will you get from asking me?

428
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:23,720
I'm going to Japan tomorrow.

429
00:29:25,040 --> 00:29:26,480
I can wait for you.

430
00:29:27,160 --> 00:29:28,480
If nothing's holding you back.

431
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:32,320
I can't take care of you.

432
00:29:33,160 --> 00:29:34,440
Look at me.

433
00:29:36,200 --> 00:29:37,560
I'm a loser.

434
00:29:39,400 --> 00:29:40,520
We're not right for each other.

435
00:29:41,560 --> 00:29:43,200
I don't care about that.

436
00:29:44,400 --> 00:29:46,080
No matter how different we are,

437
00:29:46,160 --> 00:29:48,200
I'm willing to adjust.

438
00:29:49,320 --> 00:29:51,000
I can take responsibility for your life

439
00:29:51,080 --> 00:29:52,680
and everyone in it.

440
00:29:57,160 --> 00:29:59,200
I know you get lonely.

441
00:30:00,360 --> 00:30:01,920
If you date me,

442
00:30:02,920 --> 00:30:04,200
even with a boyfriend,

443
00:30:05,040 --> 00:30:07,000
you'll still have to eat alone,

444
00:30:07,080 --> 00:30:08,560
sleep alone,

445
00:30:09,200 --> 00:30:10,440
and work on models alone.

446
00:30:11,480 --> 00:30:13,320
You won't have anyone to vent to.

447
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:16,400
- But I can call you, can't I?
- Yes, but I won't be here.

448
00:30:18,440 --> 00:30:20,960
Do you really think you can handle
a long-distance relationship?

449
00:30:27,520 --> 00:30:29,320
Choose someone who can be there for you.

450
00:30:29,400 --> 00:30:30,400
Like Kan.

451
00:30:31,480 --> 00:30:32,560
I looked into him.

452
00:30:33,480 --> 00:30:34,840
He's got everything going for him.

453
00:30:35,960 --> 00:30:37,800
His family is loaded.

454
00:30:37,880 --> 00:30:39,240
He has a future.

455
00:30:39,840 --> 00:30:41,080
His family name is well-known too.

456
00:30:41,880 --> 00:30:43,160
He can easily take care of you.

457
00:30:47,960 --> 00:30:50,080
I can't date Kan anymore.

458
00:30:51,120 --> 00:30:52,920
I only have feelings…

459
00:30:54,840 --> 00:30:56,400
for you now.

460
00:31:01,760 --> 00:31:03,280
I feel at ease

461
00:31:04,960 --> 00:31:06,560
and I feel safe

462
00:31:06,640 --> 00:31:07,840
when I'm with you.

463
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:14,560
But if I'm not here,

464
00:31:14,640 --> 00:31:16,760
that sense of comfort will change.

465
00:31:19,280 --> 00:31:21,680
I don't want the good feelings
we have today

466
00:31:21,760 --> 00:31:23,040
to turn into hate.

467
00:31:25,760 --> 00:31:27,800
I think we should stop
while things are still good.

468
00:31:40,600 --> 00:31:42,600
Then, can I have one last moment…

469
00:31:46,280 --> 00:31:47,720
with you?

470
00:33:19,920 --> 00:33:21,040
You can see me off here.

471
00:33:21,120 --> 00:33:22,520
You don't have to take me to the airport.

472
00:33:24,960 --> 00:33:27,800
When you graduate,
don't forget to invite me.

473
00:33:28,480 --> 00:33:30,040
Just think of me as a younger brother.

474
00:33:30,120 --> 00:33:32,080
I just want to congratulate you.

475
00:33:33,760 --> 00:33:34,800
Sure.

476
00:33:35,840 --> 00:33:36,880
I'll invite you.

477
00:33:40,320 --> 00:33:41,960
In two years, when I graduate,

478
00:33:42,040 --> 00:33:43,360
I'll come back here.

479
00:33:45,040 --> 00:33:46,320
By then,

480
00:33:46,920 --> 00:33:48,360
if you're still single,

481
00:33:50,960 --> 00:33:52,200
shall we date then?

482
00:33:54,520 --> 00:33:55,960
But you don't have to wait for me.

483
00:33:56,040 --> 00:33:58,080
If you find someone better than me,
go for it.

484
00:33:59,960 --> 00:34:01,840
Take good care of yourself from now on.

485
00:34:02,600 --> 00:34:04,200
Be happy, okay?

486
00:34:05,840 --> 00:34:07,600
If you want me to be happy,

487
00:34:08,960 --> 00:34:10,760
then hurry back to me.

488
00:34:18,239 --> 00:34:19,080
Well,

489
00:34:19,159 --> 00:34:20,120
I'm going.

490
00:34:20,840 --> 00:34:21,960
Wait.

491
00:34:44,600 --> 00:34:45,719
Good luck.

492
00:35:24,680 --> 00:35:26,280
THE CROW CLUB

493
00:35:32,840 --> 00:35:35,280
I thought I'd come to terms
with being apart from Vann.

494
00:35:36,440 --> 00:35:37,520
But now I know

495
00:35:37,600 --> 00:35:39,200
it's just so hard.

496
00:35:40,840 --> 00:35:42,520
He'll be back soon.

497
00:35:42,600 --> 00:35:45,400
He's just checking out the dorm
and sorting things out at the university.

498
00:35:45,480 --> 00:35:47,000
He hasn't even started studying yet.

499
00:35:47,720 --> 00:35:49,560
Knowing Vann, he'll probably stay there.

500
00:35:49,640 --> 00:35:51,360
He probably won't come back
and waste the money.

501
00:35:52,480 --> 00:35:53,760
That mouth of yours.

502
00:35:53,840 --> 00:35:56,920
You barely ever talk.
Why now? He's already upset.

503
00:35:57,440 --> 00:35:59,000
- Yeah.
- Well, it's the truth.

504
00:35:59,080 --> 00:36:01,560
You don't have to
say every truth out loud.

505
00:36:02,640 --> 00:36:03,520
Sorry.

506
00:36:05,400 --> 00:36:07,360
I don't think I can handle this.

507
00:36:08,600 --> 00:36:10,600
What am I gonna do? It's two whole years.

508
00:36:11,920 --> 00:36:13,840
What if someone hits on him?

509
00:36:15,480 --> 00:36:17,800
Don't worry about that, Rakkhun.

510
00:36:17,880 --> 00:36:19,640
Vann really only has his looks.

511
00:36:19,720 --> 00:36:21,880
When it comes to anything else,
he's clueless.

512
00:36:21,960 --> 00:36:23,760
He wouldn't even know
if someone hit on him.

513
00:36:32,320 --> 00:36:33,680
He's got it bad.

514
00:36:34,440 --> 00:36:35,360
True.

515
00:36:38,240 --> 00:36:40,520
Long-distance relationships

516
00:36:40,600 --> 00:36:42,000
really are hard.

517
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:47,160
But if I knew where I stood with him,

518
00:36:47,760 --> 00:36:49,640
maybe I could do something.

519
00:36:51,240 --> 00:36:52,920
But I can't do anything.

520
00:36:55,680 --> 00:36:57,640
I don't know
where I fit into the equation.

521
00:37:13,160 --> 00:37:14,640
<i>From now on, when you're sad,</i>

522
00:37:14,720 --> 00:37:16,080
look at this bracelet

523
00:37:16,160 --> 00:37:17,880
and think of me instead, okay?

524
00:37:25,720 --> 00:37:28,640
TOKYO, JAPAN

525
00:37:36,200 --> 00:37:38,480
You made Rakkhun sad.

526
00:37:39,880 --> 00:37:41,360
You're dead!

527
00:38:00,880 --> 00:38:03,480
Rakkhun's life was ruined
because of a man.

528
00:38:04,280 --> 00:38:05,680
You must take responsibility.

529
00:38:06,360 --> 00:38:07,560
Wait.

530
00:38:07,640 --> 00:38:09,480
Calm down. Let's talk this through.

531
00:38:09,560 --> 00:38:11,280
I just got here.

532
00:38:11,360 --> 00:38:13,240
Can't you give me time
to get over my jet lag?

533
00:38:13,320 --> 00:38:14,680
According to our deal,

534
00:38:14,760 --> 00:38:16,920
if Rakkhun gets his heart broken,

535
00:38:17,000 --> 00:38:18,120
you must die.

536
00:38:19,360 --> 00:38:21,760
Rakkhun is hurting because of you now.

537
00:38:22,280 --> 00:38:24,560
How could he be hurting because of me?

538
00:38:24,640 --> 00:38:26,240
You're just looking
for an excuse to kill me.

539
00:38:26,760 --> 00:38:28,920
I won't let you get me that easily.

540
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:30,800
Rakkhun loves you.

541
00:38:36,360 --> 00:38:38,360
Like I loved Chanta.

542
00:38:45,960 --> 00:38:47,440
<i>Walk slowly.</i>

543
00:38:47,520 --> 00:38:49,640
- Watch your step.
- Don't fall.

544
00:38:49,720 --> 00:38:53,320
<i>I once had a love like Rakkhun's too.</i>

545
00:39:01,080 --> 00:39:03,280
<i>It was all impossible.</i>

546
00:39:04,880 --> 00:39:07,000
Garlah! Chanta!

547
00:39:15,720 --> 00:39:16,720
Enough!

548
00:39:32,680 --> 00:39:33,720
Chanta.

549
00:39:37,240 --> 00:39:38,600
Chanta.

550
00:39:40,440 --> 00:39:41,400
Chanta.

551
00:39:44,040 --> 00:39:44,960
Chanta.

552
00:39:55,160 --> 00:39:56,240
Chanta.

553
00:40:00,640 --> 00:40:01,680
Chanta.

554
00:40:01,760 --> 00:40:03,640
<i>Because we loved the wrong gender,</i>

555
00:40:03,720 --> 00:40:08,240
<i>Chanta and I</i>
<i>had to suffer the consequences.</i>

556
00:40:57,360 --> 00:40:59,880
So I must protect my descendants

557
00:40:59,960 --> 00:41:01,920
from living a life like mine.

558
00:41:03,040 --> 00:41:05,560
Rakkhun is a lot like me.

559
00:41:07,040 --> 00:41:09,600
I won't let him end up like me.

560
00:41:11,120 --> 00:41:13,160
You said Rakkhun loves me, right?

561
00:41:13,760 --> 00:41:14,720
Yes.

562
00:41:15,520 --> 00:41:17,160
Rakkhun loves you.

563
00:41:17,760 --> 00:41:20,960
But his life is about to fall apart
because of you!

564
00:41:23,240 --> 00:41:25,760
What if I can make Rakkhun happy?

565
00:41:26,400 --> 00:41:29,480
If I can keep Rakkhun
from ending up like you,

566
00:41:29,560 --> 00:41:30,680
will you agree?

567
00:41:30,760 --> 00:41:32,200
Don't try to trick me.

568
00:41:42,800 --> 00:41:45,320
You said Rakkhun is like you, didn't you?

569
00:41:46,520 --> 00:41:47,880
If I die,

570
00:41:48,880 --> 00:41:51,280
he'll suffer like you did.

571
00:41:53,480 --> 00:41:55,960
I'll stake my whole life on this.

572
00:41:56,560 --> 00:41:58,360
I love Rakkhun.

573
00:42:00,680 --> 00:42:01,760
I want

574
00:42:01,840 --> 00:42:03,480
him to be happy.

575
00:42:24,040 --> 00:42:26,000
Let me take care of Rakkhun.

576
00:42:45,560 --> 00:42:49,080
Rakkhun, for the assignment the professor
wants revised, how about this topic?

577
00:42:49,160 --> 00:42:50,600
Which one? This one or this one?

578
00:42:50,680 --> 00:42:51,600
This one.

579
00:42:52,280 --> 00:42:54,160
- Or this one?
- It's interesting.

580
00:42:55,680 --> 00:42:56,840
How about this one?

581
00:42:56,920 --> 00:42:58,680
- This one looks okay too.
- Rakkhun.

582
00:43:10,440 --> 00:43:11,880
Hey,

583
00:43:11,960 --> 00:43:13,200
what are you wearing?

584
00:43:13,840 --> 00:43:15,000
Is this some new fashion?

585
00:43:19,000 --> 00:43:20,360
It's vintage.

586
00:43:21,400 --> 00:43:22,440
Well? Does it suit me?

587
00:43:23,960 --> 00:43:25,160
Well,

588
00:43:25,240 --> 00:43:26,840
it looks a little forced.

589
00:43:27,800 --> 00:43:29,320
But it's not bad.

590
00:43:34,720 --> 00:43:36,960
You still haven't finished
your assignment?

591
00:43:37,960 --> 00:43:38,800
Oh.

592
00:43:38,880 --> 00:43:40,400
The professor told us to revise it.

593
00:43:42,280 --> 00:43:44,600
What about yours? Have you done it yet?

594
00:43:44,680 --> 00:43:46,720
I'm done. Want me to help?

595
00:43:47,760 --> 00:43:50,480
For you, I'll help for free.

596
00:43:51,640 --> 00:43:53,120
I'd even help you for life.

597
00:44:00,320 --> 00:44:01,320
Kan.

598
00:44:03,360 --> 00:44:04,760
I have something to tell you.

599
00:44:06,840 --> 00:44:08,560
I want to make things clear with you.

600
00:44:17,200 --> 00:44:19,000
You don't like me anymore, do you?

601
00:44:24,960 --> 00:44:26,640
I could kind of tell.

602
00:44:28,800 --> 00:44:30,480
But do I really have no chance anymore?

603
00:44:33,640 --> 00:44:36,000
I don't feel that way about you anymore.

604
00:44:36,600 --> 00:44:37,840
I like someone else now.

605
00:44:39,560 --> 00:44:40,800
The guy…

606
00:44:41,800 --> 00:44:43,160
named Vann?

607
00:44:44,640 --> 00:44:45,640
Yes.

608
00:44:46,760 --> 00:44:48,480
I'm waiting for him to come back.

609
00:44:49,760 --> 00:44:51,080
I'll wait for him to come back.

610
00:44:53,640 --> 00:44:55,640
I can only be your friend.

611
00:44:57,240 --> 00:44:59,080
But if you can't be friends with me,

612
00:44:59,640 --> 00:45:01,000
I understand.

613
00:45:04,720 --> 00:45:06,360
I'll probably need some time.

614
00:45:32,280 --> 00:45:33,760
POWERFUL EARTHQUAKE STRIKES JAPAN

615
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:38,040
VANN

616
00:45:56,040 --> 00:45:57,400
Talay.

617
00:45:57,480 --> 00:45:59,400
Did you see the news about
the earthquake in Japan?

618
00:46:00,080 --> 00:46:02,120
It's the same city Vann is in.

619
00:46:02,200 --> 00:46:04,400
<i>Can you contact him?</i>

620
00:46:04,480 --> 00:46:06,360
He's not answering our calls either.

621
00:46:06,440 --> 00:46:09,240
Linda is contacting his dorm now.

622
00:46:09,760 --> 00:46:11,760
I'll let you know
as soon as I hear anything.

623
00:46:13,520 --> 00:46:15,600
Okay. Keep me updated.

624
00:46:15,680 --> 00:46:16,680
<i>Okay.</i>

625
00:46:30,320 --> 00:46:31,760
The flight was canceled?

626
00:46:31,840 --> 00:46:33,600
Are there any other flights?

627
00:46:34,200 --> 00:46:35,280
Okay.

628
00:46:46,040 --> 00:46:47,120
Vann!

629
00:46:53,640 --> 00:46:54,720
How are you?

630
00:46:55,240 --> 00:46:56,720
Are you hurt anywhere?

631
00:46:59,440 --> 00:47:00,320
I'm fine.

632
00:47:21,800 --> 00:47:23,280
I'm really fine.

633
00:47:23,360 --> 00:47:24,560
Why are you crying?

634
00:47:29,120 --> 00:47:32,000
I turned on my phone
and saw almost 100 missed calls.

635
00:47:32,080 --> 00:47:33,160
From you,

636
00:47:33,240 --> 00:47:35,200
Talay, and Linda.

637
00:47:35,760 --> 00:47:37,640
My phone was about to explode.

638
00:47:37,720 --> 00:47:39,960
Well, everyone was worried about you.

639
00:47:40,040 --> 00:47:42,280
We thought you might've
died in the earthquake.

640
00:47:45,080 --> 00:47:46,880
When the earthquake hit,

641
00:47:46,960 --> 00:47:48,960
I thought I was going to die too.

642
00:47:49,040 --> 00:47:50,880
You can still joke about it?

643
00:47:54,200 --> 00:47:55,800
When I took cover under a table

644
00:47:56,560 --> 00:47:58,080
and the building shook,

645
00:47:58,160 --> 00:48:00,360
the ceiling came crashing down
right in front of me.

646
00:48:01,720 --> 00:48:03,560
My mind suddenly went blank.

647
00:48:06,360 --> 00:48:07,680
You were the first person I thought of.

648
00:48:10,320 --> 00:48:11,560
Before I knew it,

649
00:48:12,640 --> 00:48:15,360
I'd booked the first flight
back to Thailand to see you.

650
00:48:17,400 --> 00:48:18,600
You did the right thing.

651
00:48:19,120 --> 00:48:20,720
You made the right choice.

652
00:48:22,760 --> 00:48:23,880
I don't think

653
00:48:25,160 --> 00:48:27,440
we're cut out for
a long-distance relationship.

654
00:48:29,600 --> 00:48:30,600
Why?

655
00:48:36,880 --> 00:48:38,760
But I want to take a chance.

656
00:48:39,360 --> 00:48:41,080
There's nothing more regrettable than

657
00:48:41,160 --> 00:48:42,920
deciding without even trying.

658
00:48:45,800 --> 00:48:47,000
I want to be your boyfriend.

659
00:48:48,240 --> 00:48:49,200
Can I?

660
00:49:07,560 --> 00:49:08,600
You're speechless.

661
00:49:11,040 --> 00:49:13,120
Rakkhun, will you be my boyfriend?

662
00:49:15,320 --> 00:49:16,280
Yes.

663
00:49:17,600 --> 00:49:19,880
So, we're boyfriends now, right?

664
00:49:20,720 --> 00:49:21,600
Yes.

665
00:49:24,400 --> 00:49:25,760
But before we tell anyone,

666
00:49:26,360 --> 00:49:28,040
there's something you need to know.

667
00:49:28,120 --> 00:49:30,720
I made a deal with Garlah, staking my life

668
00:49:30,800 --> 00:49:32,440
so she'd let you go.

669
00:49:33,600 --> 00:49:34,760
I told her

670
00:49:35,600 --> 00:49:37,520
if you get your heart broken
because of a man,

671
00:49:37,600 --> 00:49:39,360
I'd let her kill me.

672
00:49:39,960 --> 00:49:41,680
Why would you do that?

673
00:49:42,800 --> 00:49:44,880
If she takes your life,

674
00:49:45,480 --> 00:49:46,720
how am I supposed to live?

675
00:49:48,800 --> 00:49:50,160
When I saw her,

676
00:49:51,280 --> 00:49:53,520
I realized how much you were suffering.

677
00:49:55,280 --> 00:49:56,120
Rakkhun.

678
00:49:56,800 --> 00:50:00,200
Now I know I'm the only one
who can make you happy.

679
00:50:05,720 --> 00:50:07,200
That's so fucking touching, right?

680
00:50:08,240 --> 00:50:10,160
You're so extreme.

681
00:50:10,760 --> 00:50:13,240
When you act like this, it's not cute.

682
00:50:13,920 --> 00:50:17,120
If I'm like this, will you still love me?

683
00:50:20,280 --> 00:50:21,200
Of course.

684
00:50:21,840 --> 00:50:23,120
I love you so much.

685
00:50:24,840 --> 00:50:26,680
If you ever leave me,

686
00:50:27,440 --> 00:50:29,520
I'll have Garlah snap your neck.

687
00:51:25,640 --> 00:51:27,880
I hope this love of yours

688
00:51:29,160 --> 00:51:30,800
brings you happiness.

689
00:51:30,880 --> 00:51:31,880
Rakkhun.

690
00:51:34,640 --> 00:51:35,480
Vann,

691
00:51:35,560 --> 00:51:36,480
are you okay?

692
00:51:38,480 --> 00:51:39,720
I thought I heard something.

693
00:51:40,640 --> 00:51:41,640
I must've imagined it.

694
00:51:58,880 --> 00:51:59,960
Hey, Vann.

695
00:52:01,400 --> 00:52:03,200
There was an earthquake.
You didn't answer my calls,

696
00:52:03,280 --> 00:52:05,240
but you just show up here?

697
00:52:05,320 --> 00:52:06,240
What?

698
00:52:06,320 --> 00:52:08,560
I already talked to Linda.

699
00:52:08,640 --> 00:52:09,960
Right, Linda?

700
00:52:10,640 --> 00:52:12,400
He's just making a fuss.

701
00:52:12,480 --> 00:52:13,680
I knew.

702
00:52:14,920 --> 00:52:17,160
Didn't you say you'd be back in two years?

703
00:52:18,800 --> 00:52:20,240
I shouldn't have cried over you.

704
00:52:24,160 --> 00:52:25,760
Whoa.

705
00:52:30,960 --> 00:52:34,680
So the bracelet I gave you really worked.

706
00:52:34,760 --> 00:52:36,720
Why did you come back, though?

707
00:52:37,440 --> 00:52:39,000
I just came to get some documents.

708
00:52:39,520 --> 00:52:42,440
Once I submit them, that's it.

709
00:52:45,640 --> 00:52:47,880
Just admit you missed us.

710
00:52:47,960 --> 00:52:49,360
You dinosaur.

711
00:52:52,120 --> 00:52:53,680
He doesn't mean us.

712
00:52:54,360 --> 00:52:56,400
He missed Rakkhun.

713
00:52:56,920 --> 00:52:58,080
Of course.

714
00:52:58,160 --> 00:53:01,000
Of course I missed my boyfriend
more than you guys.

715
00:53:02,640 --> 00:53:04,000
Okay.

716
00:53:04,080 --> 00:53:06,960
Wait, are you guys dating now?

717
00:53:07,040 --> 00:53:09,760
Who asked who out first?

718
00:53:10,400 --> 00:53:11,360
Hey.

719
00:53:11,440 --> 00:53:14,480
Tell us everything. Every last detail.

720
00:53:15,680 --> 00:53:17,680
Want me to write you a report?

721
00:53:17,760 --> 00:53:18,760
That would be nice.

722
00:53:19,800 --> 00:53:21,480
Just knowing we're dating is enough.

723
00:53:22,640 --> 00:53:24,440
Linda!

724
00:53:24,520 --> 00:53:27,000
Someone broke the rules.
Shouldn't he be kicked out?

725
00:53:35,680 --> 00:53:38,800
If breaking the rules helps
the Crows learn,

726
00:53:39,640 --> 00:53:40,760
I'm okay with it.

727
00:53:42,080 --> 00:53:44,680
Because now, Rakkhun

728
00:53:44,760 --> 00:53:47,880
is part of our Crow Club family.

729
00:53:50,360 --> 00:53:52,200
Take good care of Rakkhun.

730
00:53:52,960 --> 00:53:54,520
He's better than you at everything,

731
00:53:54,600 --> 00:53:56,000
and he still chose you.

732
00:53:56,080 --> 00:53:57,320
Don't let him down.

733
00:53:57,400 --> 00:53:58,640
Hey.

734
00:53:58,720 --> 00:54:00,320
I'm your little brother, remember?

735
00:54:00,400 --> 00:54:02,000
You should be tough on him.

736
00:54:02,080 --> 00:54:04,160
Like a big brother
protecting his little brother.

737
00:54:04,760 --> 00:54:05,680
Why would we be protective of you?

738
00:54:06,280 --> 00:54:07,920
If Rakkhun doesn't want you, no one will.

739
00:54:09,360 --> 00:54:10,560
That's true.

740
00:54:10,640 --> 00:54:13,280
I never thought someone like you
could get a boyfriend.

741
00:54:15,280 --> 00:54:16,480
So I got myself a rare one?

742
00:54:17,920 --> 00:54:19,320
Limited edition.

743
00:54:20,400 --> 00:54:22,440
While I'm in Japan,
take care of Rakkhun for me.

744
00:54:22,520 --> 00:54:25,840
If anyone hits on him, beat them up.
You have my permission.

745
00:54:27,680 --> 00:54:29,280
- Calm down.
- Okay.

746
00:54:32,560 --> 00:54:35,480
Vann. About the deal you made with Garlah…

747
00:54:35,560 --> 00:54:38,040
She won't come back
for your life later, right?

748
00:54:38,640 --> 00:54:39,720
No.

749
00:54:39,800 --> 00:54:41,640
If I don't hurt you, she won't come.

750
00:54:42,280 --> 00:54:44,400
And I'd never do that anyway.

751
00:54:45,440 --> 00:54:47,080
That's easy to say now.

752
00:54:47,960 --> 00:54:50,280
We'll have to see what happens
from now on.

753
00:54:50,960 --> 00:54:52,480
Then keep watching.

754
00:54:54,120 --> 00:54:57,440
Thank you for never letting go of me.

755
00:55:01,840 --> 00:55:04,240
Can you say what you just said again?

756
00:55:04,840 --> 00:55:05,880
Which part?

757
00:55:05,960 --> 00:55:07,400
When I told them

758
00:55:07,480 --> 00:55:09,480
if anyone hits on you,
they can beat them up?

759
00:55:09,560 --> 00:55:10,680
No.

760
00:55:11,400 --> 00:55:13,640
What you said we are.

761
00:55:19,640 --> 00:55:22,040
You're the only boyfriend I love.

762
00:55:25,520 --> 00:55:27,160
I love you, Rakkhun.

763
00:56:59,880 --> 00:57:01,280
Someone once told me,

764
00:57:01,360 --> 00:57:03,240
if I can't write
what I want to write right now,

765
00:57:03,320 --> 00:57:04,680
I should write something else first.

766
00:57:04,760 --> 00:57:06,480
<i>Want to have some fun with adult fiction?</i>

767
00:57:06,560 --> 00:57:08,040
<i>What happened to your hand?</i>

768
00:57:08,120 --> 00:57:09,280
Who did this to you? Tell me.

769
00:57:09,360 --> 00:57:10,840
<i>Why do you care about me?</i>

770
00:57:10,920 --> 00:57:12,680
Vann really doesn't have
someone else, right?

771
00:57:12,760 --> 00:57:14,960
I've gone through three decks already.

772
00:57:15,040 --> 00:57:17,560
<i>Vann could never pull anyone else anyway.</i>

773
00:57:17,640 --> 00:57:21,480
I told you, if you can't find
a main vocalist with a distinctive voice,

774
00:57:21,560 --> 00:57:23,280
I don't know why you should debut.

775
00:57:23,360 --> 00:57:24,400
<i>If he doesn't join us,</i>

776
00:57:24,480 --> 00:57:25,840
<i>we'll have to change our plans.</i>

777
00:57:25,920 --> 00:57:26,800
Trust me.

778
00:57:26,880 --> 00:57:29,800
<i>This time, he'll definitely say yes.</i>
